# Source is text, and must be DIFFED as text.
#
# Git auto-detects "binary" from a NUL byte, and a file it thinks is binary is
# shown in review as "Binary files differ" — no lines, no diff, no review. A
# single stray control byte in a TypeScript file has done exactly that three
# times in this repo, twice hiding ~19KB of security tests from a review diff
# and once hiding a filename-validation regex in src/files/r2.ts.
#
# Both attributes are load-bearing and they do different jobs:
#   text  — normalizes line endings.
#   diff  — forces a TEXTUAL diff, overriding the NUL-byte auto-detection.
#           `text` alone does NOT do this, which is the subtlety that makes
#           this failure keep coming back.
#
# The matching machine guard that FAILS on the byte, rather than merely
# rendering it, is apps/worker/scripts/check-text-files.mjs, wired into the
# `codemode:dts:check` script.

*.ts    text diff
*.tsx   text diff
*.js    text diff
*.mjs   text diff
*.cjs   text diff
*.json  text diff
*.jsonc text diff
*.md    text diff
*.sql   text diff
*.yml   text diff
*.yaml  text diff
*.css   text diff
*.html  text diff
*.sh    text diff eol=lf
